---
import "../../styles/surfaces.css";
import DocsPage from "../../components/DocsPage.astro";
import ChartMount from "../../components/ChartMount.astro";
import { loadTheming } from "../../lib/batch3";

const page = loadTheming();
const description = "Soft is the default ChartKit look. Switch refined, editorial, and midnight, or derive a palette from a brand colour.";
const lightCss = `.chart-host {
  --ck-background: transparent;
  --ck-text: #1d1d1f;
  --ck-muted: #6e6e73;
  --ck-grid: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.06);
  --ck-positive: #047857;
  --ck-negative: #be123c;
  --ck-font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
}

.dark .chart-host {
  --ck-text: #f5f5f7;
  --ck-muted: #98989d;
  --ck-grid: rgb(245 245 247 / 0.08);
  --ck-positive: #30d158;
  --ck-negative: #ff453a;
}`;
const shadcn = `.chart-host {
  --ck-series-1: var(--chart-1);
  --ck-series-2: var(--chart-2);
  --ck-series-3: var(--chart-3);
  --ck-series-4: var(--chart-4);
  --ck-series-5: var(--chart-5);
}`;
const tokens = `{
  "version": "1",
  "type": "bar",
  "theme": {
    "tokens": {
      "series": ["#007aff", "#34c759", "#ff9500", "#af52de"]
    }
  }
}`;
const brand = `import { paletteFromBrand } from "@chartkitdev/core/themes/brand";

const series = paletteFromBrand("#007aff", "light");
const spec = { version: "1", type: "bar", theme: { tokens: { series } } };`;
---

<DocsPage title="Theming" description={description} href="/docs/theming">
  <p>
    Soft is the default. Omit <code>theme</code>, or set <code>"auto"</code> or <code>"soft"</code>. The plot is transparent and the colours follow the page: <code>light-dark()</code> tracks <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> and an ancestor's <code>color-scheme</code>. The optional card is <code>#f5f5f7</code> in light and <code>#1c1c1e</code> in dark. <code>--ck-*</code> still overrides, and <code>--chart-N</code> is the next fallback.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>refined</code> and <code>editorial</code> are built-in names. <code>theme: "midnight"</code> is the opt-in dark card. Any other name still falls through to midnight until you import that preset from <code>@chartkitdev/core/themes/all</code>.
  </p>
  <div data-looks>
    <div class="look-switch" role="group" aria-label="Chart look">
      {
        page.looks.map((look) => (
          <button type="button" class={look.id === "soft" ? "btn btn-primary" : "btn btn-secondary"} aria-pressed={look.id === "soft" ? "true" : "false"} data-look-id={look.id}>
            {look.label}
          </button>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="meta" data-look-detail>{page.looks[0]?.detail}</p>
    {
      page.looks.map((look) => (
        <div class={`look-stage look-${look.id}`} data-look={look.id} data-detail={look.detail} hidden={look.id === "soft" ? undefined : true}>
          <div class="look-grid">
            {look.charts.map((chart) => (
              <ChartMount spec={chart.spec} svg={chart.svg} alt={chart.alt} preset />
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p>This next chart leaves <code>theme</code> unset, so it is Soft with this page's text and grid tokens on top.</p>
  <ChartMount spec={page.swatch.spec} svg={page.swatch.svg} alt={page.swatch.alt} />
  <h2>Tokens</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="opt-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Variable</th>
          <th>Role</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          page.tokens.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{row.token}</code></td>
              <td>{row.role}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h2>Light and dark</h2>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>css</figcaption><pre><code>{lightCss}</code></pre></figure>
  <p>
    Muted text has to clear 4.5:1 against the page. Midnight's <code>#8a8a8a</code> does not, on white, so the page default is <code>auto</code> and the host sets <code>--ck-muted</code>. Point the series variables at a shadcn palette:
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>css</figcaption><pre><code>{shadcn}</code></pre></figure>
  <h2>theme.tokens.series</h2>
  <p>
    A spec can replace the series list without a preset name. The base stays Soft unless you set <code>preset</code>. <code>lines</code> defaults to the same list, so thin strokes follow the fills unless you pass a darker set.
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>json</figcaption><pre><code>{tokens}</code></pre></figure>
  <h2>paletteFromBrand</h2>
  <p>
    <code>paletteFromBrand</code> is opt-in. It is not in the line bundle and it is not the default theme. Pass one hex colour, or a list, and <code>"light"</code> or <code>"dark"</code>. Put the result on <code>theme.tokens.series</code>.
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>ts</figcaption><pre><code>{brand}</code></pre></figure>
  <div data-brand>
    <div class="brand-row">
      <label>
        Brand colour
        <input type="color" value="#007aff" aria-label="Brand colour" />
      </label>
      <p class="meta" data-brand-caption>
        <code>paletteFromBrand("#007aff", "light")</code> from <code>@chartkitdev/core/themes/brand</code>. The page scheme picks light or dark. Every colour clears 3:1 on white or on <code>#09090b</code>, not on this card.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="status" data-brand-status hidden></p>
    <div class="swatches" data-brand-swatches aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="ck-frame" data-brand-chart></div>
  </div>
  <h2>Dashboards</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/dashboards">dashboard pages</a> set series, text, grid, positive, and negative on <code>theme.tokens</code>. Each board has a light and a dark token object. Page CSS styles the shell. Fonts are Inter or Roboto. ChartKit is not affiliated with those products. Gaps that still need a spec option are in <code>catalog/dashboards/GAPS.md</code>.
  </p>
  <h2>Presets</h2>
  <p>
    Soft, refined, editorial, and midnight are built in. <a href="/docs/themes/tape">Tape</a>, <a href="/docs/themes/kite">Kite</a>, <a href="/docs/themes/mustard">Mustard</a>, and <a href="/docs/themes/violet">Violet</a> register with the older names ({page.themes.join(", ")}) when you import <code>@chartkitdev/core/themes/all</code>. <a href="/docs/themes/from-brand">A brand hex</a> or <a href="/docs/themes/from-drawing">a drawing</a> can derive a preset. Several of the older muted colours are under 4.5:1 on their own background, which is why Soft is the default.
  </p>
</DocsPage>

<script>
  import "../../scripts/mount-charts.ts";
  import "../../scripts/theme-board.ts";
  import "../../scripts/brand-palette.ts";
</script>
